# Segments, the bundle's own icon, is left to the Dock, which draws it in the icon style picked in System Settings ▸
# Appearance (Dark, Clear, Tinted) as it does every app's. 0.1.55 gave the Dock Segments' picture, which the Dock draws
# as it is, so Cra's icon stayed light in a dark Dock (GitHub #739). A pick is given to the Dock (given=<id>), and
# picking Segments after it hands the tile back (given=none). Only a launch that finds a Finder icon an earlier Cra put
# on Cra.app (#724) gives Segments too, since the Dock's cache can still hold the pick that was on it (Victor, 23 Nov
# 2026: Segments after Original kept Original); the launch after that leaves it to the Dock again. A launch with
# Segments never sets applicationIconImage (sets=0): even set to nil it hands the Dock a picture of the bundle's icon,
# which the Dock draws outside the icon style.
# Segments comes in through the argument domain and appIcon= picks without remembering, so the run never writes the
# defaults the installed Cra reads. A relaunch drops the argument, so Segments is picked again after each.
# promise: #739
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
arg -appIcon
arg segments
cra://debug?dockTile=launch
expect-log dock tile launch: view=none .* sets=0 given=none$

cra://debug?appIcon=original
cra://debug?dockTile=original
expect-log dock tile original: .* given=original$

cra://debug?appIcon=segments
cra://debug?dockTile=segments
expect-log dock tile segments: .* given=none$

# A Finder icon 0.1.54 or 0.1.55 left on the app: the launch that takes it off gives the Dock Segments' picture.
cra://debug?bundleIconPut=original
expect-log app icon: original put on the app for a test
relaunch
expect-log app icon: \S+ taken off the app
cra://debug?appIcon=segments
cra://debug?dockTile=stale
expect-log dock tile stale: .* given=segments$
relaunch
cra://debug?appIcon=segments
cra://debug?dockTile=clean
expect-log dock tile clean: .* given=none$
